WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.920
...all the way from Switzerland -
here's Frida.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.440
Hello.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.160
-Welcome.
-Thank you.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.800
When it was known that you'd be here, 
we started getting calls from all over.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.200
-It's really...
-Good thing you're answer them...

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.040
I've been on the phone the whole week,
but...

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.520
They all call to know when we'll hear
some new music from you.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.480
I've learnt never to say never.
You just don't know.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:54.320
But I've reached an age when you start
taking it easier.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.000
But I enjoy singing.
I still sing - at home.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.080
I've done a small experiment.
I live in Zermatt.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:08.120
And next year, Zermatt will celebrate
the 150th anniversary-

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.400
-of the first ascent of the Matterhorn.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.120
-That big mountain.
-Right.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.040
So, we've organized a tribute
to the Matterhorn.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:23.720
It's us and some German producers
and sound engineers.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.080
-So, it's a song about...
-About Matterhorn.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:32.240
It's called "1865".
That's when the first ascent took place.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.880
-And you're singing.
-I'm participating in it, yes.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.000
-And how's that working out?
-I don't remember right now.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:47.560
-It will be released in December.
-Is it "Ain't No Mountain high enough"?

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:51.880
No, it's not that type of song.
It's cuter.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:56.120
The mountains are 
very important to you.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.320
-You live in Switzerland.
-Yes.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:03.000
I've thought about it. I was born 
in the mountains, near Narvik.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.240
There are some very high 
mountains there too.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.880
It's as if the circle's closed now.
I'm back in the nature where I was born.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.160
I'm very happy in the mountains.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.680
I like sports, hiking, skiing,
mountain-climbing...

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.360
Well, I don't do that too often anymore.
Everything connected to nature-

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.520
-gives me peace of mind.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.480
-How much of a Swiss are you now?
-I feel at home there.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.800
I've lived in Switzerland
for 30 years now.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:41.040
It's almost as long as I lived in
Scandinavia, soon, in a couple of years.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.480
So...yes.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:49.800
I also know, that when you're 
not climbing mountains...

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:53.200
It's been a couple of years now...
Not anymore.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:58.640
One thing we learnt
during the research...

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.200
-...was that you write a lot.
-Yes.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:07.480
I've always written a lot, even though
I haven't published anything.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:12.240
But I've had to write my thoughts
out of my system-

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.160
-at times in my life when things
have been a bit harder.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:21.520
Today, my writing is more focused
on telling a story-

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.680
-rather than exploring my life.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:30.280
But I've involved myself - as an animal,
however. I won't tell you which animal.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.840
And I find this very exciting.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.320
I want to write a story
with ecological overtones-

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.520
-since I've spent a lot of time working
on this before-

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:48.680
-and still feel close to nature.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:54.480
When you say you've dealt
with difficult things in your life...

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:59.720
There's a Norwegian expression: "You've
been out during the winter's nights."

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:05.760
-Yes.
-You've suffered great hardships.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:11.040
You've had to start over quite often.
You're twice divorced.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:16.040
And you've been left a widow. And you
lost your daughter in an accident.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.080
And you've moved around a lot.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.160
You were born in Norway.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.240
-But you didn't stay there very long.
-No.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:30.200
I lived there until I was two years old.
Excuse me.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.880
The person who started my nomadic life
was my grandmother.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:38.840
She's the one who brought me
to Sweden. She'd lost her husband.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.960
She had six children
who'd already left home.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.400
She wanted to start over,
so she brought me with her.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:53.760
My mother had to move somewhere 
else in Norway to earn a living...

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:57.080
-Your father was a German soldier.
-Exactly.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.400
-He wasn't in the picture.
-Not easy in Norway.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:05.600
No, it wasn't. I can't describe the
situation back then, as I was so young.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:09.080
But she moved to Sweden and got a job-

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.000
-and that's how my nomadic life began.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.960
I have moved quite a lot.
Things have improved now.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:25.920
I used to get restless if I stayed too
long in one place. It's in my blood.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:31.040
What are your thoughts
on this breaking up and moving-

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.360
-that you were into earlier?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.240
How has this influenced
your personality?

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.920
It may have led to a certain degree
of loneliness.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:46.240
A travelling nomad is relatively lonely.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.440
This has accompanied me through life.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:54.040
A loneliness that I sometimes would
find troublesome-

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:58.880
-but that I've come to enjoy
quite a lot now.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:04.600
Solitude has become my companion.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:09.440
You told us about your grandmother
who was Norwegian.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:15.400
Where I grew up, we...
Maybe it was a bit too emphasized-

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:18.120
-that you were Norwegian.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:24.400
So, even if you were unaware of this,
ABBA was a Norwegian-Swedish band.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:29.040
It was a huge Norwegian-Swedish success,
and abroad we'd say:

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:33.280
"They are Norwegian.
Yes, they are Norwegian."

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:39.080
-So you bragged about me?
-You were my only joker abroad.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.600
-But...
-I'll disappoint you now.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:47.440
I applied for Swedish citizenship
when I was sixteen years old.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.840
I've been a Swede ever since.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:57.000
If ever you were to change your mind
I'm sure you'd be welcome here.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:03.560
But... Your grandmother.
Today you're a grandmother yourself.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.120
-Yes.
-Are you like her?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.840
-Well...
-She was an important person.

